IMPORT prelude

-- Sand and Granite Quarries Act 1970 (Singapore) -- what counts as a sand or granite quarry (s 2), the licence requirement and
-- its evidential presumptions (s 4), grant, refusal, term, transfer and appeal (ss 5, 8), recovery of works expenses (ss 7, 9, 22),
-- the fresh-water rules (ss 10, 12), the fencing offence for disused quarries (s 14), and the penalty provisions (ss 4, 9, 14,
-- 16 to 20).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SGQA1970.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest
-- amendment annotated in the text is Act 5 of 2025 (wef 09/03/2025), on the Licensing Officer (ss 2, 3). The retrieval
-- metadata calls it the "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0118 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short (24 sections), so this row covers nearly all of it. Not encoded: the appointment of the
-- Licensing Officer (s 3), security (s 6) beyond its use in recovering expenses, the Licensing Officer's direction powers on
-- waste, safety and blasting (ss 11, 13) beyond their enforcement through ss 17 and 18, the power of entry (s 15), the saving of
-- other prosecutions (s 21) and regulations (s 24). No regulations, fee schedule or exemption order was retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Sand and Granite Quarries Act 1970 -- quarries`

§§ `2 -- what a quarry is`

-- s 2: "'granite quarry' means any land from which granite blocks, gravel, stones and overburden are extracted by blasting,
-- sorting, breaking, loading and transporting, WHETHER the processes are executed by manual labour OR mechanical means";
-- "'sand quarry' means any land on which PERSONS ARE EMPLOYED IN MANUAL LABOUR in any process for or incidental to the getting,
-- dressing or preparation for the sale or otherwise of sand, gravel or earth."
--
-- The two definitions are not parallel. A granite quarry is one however worked; a sand quarry needs persons employed in manual
-- labour. Whether a machine operator is "employed in manual labour" the text does not say; here it is a fact given.
GIVEN `sand, gravel or earth is got or prepared there` IS A BOOLEAN, `persons are employed there in manual labour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the land is a sand quarry` IF
    `sand, gravel or earth is got or prepared there` AND `persons are employed there in manual labour`

GIVEN `granite, gravel, stones and overburden are extracted there` IS A BOOLEAN, `the work is manual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the land is a granite quarry` IF
    `granite, gravel, stones and overburden are extracted there`

§§ `4, 23 -- quarrying without a licence`

-- s 4(1): "No person shall ... use or manage any land for the purposes of a sand or granite quarry without a licence from the
-- Licensing Officer". (2): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a fine not exceeding $100
-- for every day or part thereof during which the offence continues after conviction."
-- s 23: "The Minister may by order exempt any sand or granite quarry from all or any of the provisions of this Act."
GIVEN `uses or manages land as a quarry` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the quarry is exempted by order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `quarrying without a licence is an offence` IF
    `uses or manages land as a quarry` AND (NOT `holds a licence`) AND (NOT `the quarry is exempted by order`)

-- s 4(3): in a prosecution, (a) "the existence in or on any land of any apparatus or accessories for the getting, dressing or
-- preparation ... of sand" is prima facie evidence that "the person owning or having the control of such apparatus" has been
-- using or managing the land as a sand quarry; (b) the same for "mechanical equipment ... used for the purpose of extracting
-- granite blocks" and a granite quarry.
--
-- The presumption falls on whoever owns OR controls the equipment, not on the landowner as such. It is prima facie only.
DECLARE Kind IS ONE OF
    `a sand quarry`
    `a granite quarry`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A Kind, `sand apparatus is on the land` IS A BOOLEAN, `granite extraction equipment is on the land` IS A BOOLEAN, `owns or controls it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `use as that kind of quarry is presumed` IF
    `owns or controls it` AND
        CONSIDER `the kind`
        WHEN `a sand quarry` THEN `sand apparatus is on the land`
        WHEN `a granite quarry` THEN `granite extraction equipment is on the land`

§§ `5, 8 -- grant, term, transfer and appeal`

-- s 5(1), (2): the Licensing Officer "may at his discretion grant, renew or refuse any licence ... without any reason ... being
-- assigned". But three things BAR a grant:
--   s 5(3): if an applicant refuses to furnish information reasonably required, the Licensing Officer "SHALL refuse";
--   s 5(7): "No licence for carrying on any granite quarry shall be granted unless the applicant ... deposits ... a certified
--   site plan from the Chief Surveyor";
--   s 8: "No licence shall be granted unless the Licensing Officer is satisfied that the use ... will be unlikely (a) to cause
--   any nuisance or damage to occupants of adjoining or neighbouring land or buildings; (b) to cause depreciation in the value
--   or amenity of adjoining or neighbouring land or buildings; or (c) to be dangerous to health, life or property."
--
-- Meeting all three gives no right to a licence; it only means a grant is not barred. s 8 speaks of grant, not renewal; s 5(3)
-- covers both. The renewal point is not modelled.
DECLARE Application HAS
    `the kind of quarry` IS A Kind
    `refused information required` IS A BOOLEAN
    `deposited a Chief Surveyor's certified site plan` IS A BOOLEAN
    `likely to cause nuisance or damage to neighbours` IS A BOOLEAN
    `likely to depreciate neighbouring value or amenity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `likely to be dangerous to health, life or property` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the site plan rule is met` IF
    CONSIDER `the application`'s `the kind of quarry`
    WHEN `a granite quarry` THEN `the application`'s `deposited a Chief Surveyor's certified site plan`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Licensing Officer may grant the licence` IF
        (NOT `the application`'s `refused information required`)
    AND `the site plan rule is met` `the application`
    AND (NOT `the application`'s `likely to cause nuisance or damage to neighbours`)
    AND (NOT `the application`'s `likely to depreciate neighbouring value or amenity`)
    AND (NOT `the application`'s `likely to be dangerous to health, life or property`)

-- s 5(4): "Except as otherwise expressly provided in the licence, any licence ... may be for such period NOT EXCEEDING 12 MONTHS".
-- s 5(6): "No such licence shall be transferable without the consent of the Licensing Officer."
GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER, `the licence expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence period is within section 5(4)` IF
    `the licence expressly provides otherwise` OR `months` AT MOST 12

GIVEN `the Licensing Officer consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence may be transferred` IF
    `the Licensing Officer consented`

-- s 5(2): a licence is "subject to suspension or revocation at any time WITHOUT COMPENSATION and WITHOUT NOTICE by the Licensing
-- Officer upon breach of any restriction or condition".
GIVEN `a restriction or condition was breached` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence may be suspended or revoked without notice` IF
    `a restriction or condition was breached`

-- s 5(8): "Any person aggrieved by the REFUSAL ... to grant or renew any licence or by the SUSPENSION or REVOCATION ... may within
-- ONE MONTH of the refusal, suspension or revocation appeal to the Minister whose decision shall be FINAL."
--
-- The list is closed: no appeal is given against the restrictions and conditions attached to a grant (s 5(2)), or against a
-- refusal of consent to transfer (s 5(6)).
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `a refusal to grant`
    `a refusal to renew`
    `a suspension`
    `a revocation`
    `conditions attached to a grant`
    `a refusal of consent to transfer`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision, `lodged within one month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the Minister lies` IF
    `lodged within one month` AND
        CONSIDER `the decision`
        WHEN `a refusal to grant` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a refusal to renew` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a suspension` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a revocation` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `7, 9, 22 -- works done in default, and recovering the cost`

-- s 7(2) (works to prevent nuisance or danger) and s 9(3) (restoring a river bank): after the time in the notice expires the
-- Licensing Officer may, "WITHOUT INSTITUTING ANY PROCEEDINGS", do the work, and the expenses "may be recovered (a) by deducting
-- the amount due from any sum deposited by the licensee as security under section 6; or (b) in the manner provided in section 22."
-- s 22(2): "If the amount ... is not paid ... within 7 DAYS after demand, the amount may be reported to a Magistrate's Court and
-- recovered in the same way as if it were a FINE".
GIVEN `the notice period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN, `the licensee complied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Licensing Officer may do the work at the licensee's expense` IF
    `the notice period has expired` AND (NOT `the licensee complied`)

GIVEN `days since demand` IS A NUMBER, `paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the expenses may be recovered as if a fine` IF
    (NOT `paid`) AND `days since demand` GREATER THAN 7

§§ `10, 12 -- fresh water`

-- s 10(1): "Every licensee shall ONLY use fresh water in connection with his sand quarrying operations" and ensure the water is
-- freed of mud, sand, silt or other refuse likely to interfere with natural flow before it leaves the area. (3): complying with a
-- notice to build spillways, dams or settling pits "shall NOT affect any liability incurred ... through breach of subsection (1)".
-- s 12: "No licensee shall without the WRITTEN permission of the Licensing Officer use any method of removing or excavating sand
-- by the direct action of fresh water."
--
-- Neither section carries its own penalty; breach falls to the general penalty in s 18.
GIVEN `used only fresh water` IS A BOOLEAN, `the water left the area freed of mud and silt` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied with a section 10(2) notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee breaches section 10(1)` IF
    (NOT `used only fresh water`) OR (NOT `the water left the area freed of mud and silt`)

GIVEN `excavates sand by the direct action of fresh water` IS A BOOLEAN, `has written permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee breaches section 12` IF
    `excavates sand by the direct action of fresh water` AND (NOT `has written permission`)

§§ `14 -- disused quarries`

-- s 14: "Where any DISUSED sand or granite quarry is dangerous to the public, it shall be kept reasonably fenced ... and if it is
-- not so kept, the LICENSEE ... or IF THERE IS NO SUCH LICENSEE THE OWNER OF THE LAND ... shall be guilty of an offence".
GIVEN `the quarry is disused` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is dangerous to the public` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is reasonably fenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disused quarry is in breach of section 14` IF
    `the quarry is disused` AND `it is dangerous to the public` AND (NOT `it is reasonably fenced`)

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `the licensee`
    `the owner of the land`

GIVEN `there is a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Person
`who is liable under section 14` MEANS
    IF `there is a licensee` THEN `the licensee` ELSE `the owner of the land`

§§ `4, 9, 14, 16 to 19 -- penalties`

-- s 4(2) unlicensed quarrying: $5,000, and $100 a day continuing after conviction.
-- s 9(2) failing to restore a river bank on notice: $1,000, and $50 a day.
-- s 14 an unfenced dangerous disused quarry: $1,000, and $50 a day.
-- s 16 obstructing an officer or removing a level mark: "a fine not exceeding $1,000 OR to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- one year" -- the only imprisonment in the Act.
-- s 17(1) default on a notice, order or direction "where no fine is specially provided for such default": $1,000 -- with NO daily
-- sum.
-- s 18 any other contravention or "breach of the conditions or restrictions" of a licence "for which no penalty is expressly
-- provided": $1,000, and $50 a day.
-- s 19: an attempt or abetment carries "the punishment provided for that offence".
--
-- Reading: a notice default under s 17 has a penalty "expressly provided", so s 18's daily sum does not reach it. The days
-- counted are days "or part thereof" during which the offence continues AFTER conviction.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `unlicensed quarrying`
    `failing to restore a river bank`
    `leaving a dangerous disused quarry unfenced`
    `obstructing an officer`
    `defaulting on a notice with no special fine`
    `any other contravention or breach of licence condition`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed quarrying` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 1000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum daily fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed quarrying` THEN 100
    WHEN `failing to restore a river bank` THEN 50
    WHEN `leaving a dangerous disused quarry unfenced` THEN 50
    WHEN `any other contravention or breach of licence condition` THEN 50
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum total fine` MEANS
    `the maximum fine` `the offence` PLUS `the maximum daily fine` `the offence` TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

-- s 16 "or": a fine or imprisonment, not both (a literal reading).
GIVEN `fine` IS A NUMBER, `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sentence is within section 16` IF
        (`fine` AT MOST 1000 AND `months` EQUALS 0)
    OR  (`fine` EQUALS 0 AND `months` AT MOST 12)

§§ `20 -- the licensee answers for staff`

-- s 20(1): a licensee liable to a pecuniary penalty for an act or default "shall be liable to the same pecuniary penalty ... for
-- every similar act ... of any agent or servant employed by him in the course of his business as such licensee". (2): "Every
-- person who APPEARS to be employed in any sand or granite quarry licensed under this Act shall ... be deemed to be a servant of
-- the licensee". (3): the agent or servant is not relieved.
--
-- No defence of due diligence or lack of knowledge appears in the section.
GIVEN `the act would be an offence by the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN, `done by an agent or servant` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the course of the licensee's business` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person appears to be employed at the licensed quarry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee is liable for the act` IF
        `the act would be an offence by the licensee`
    AND (`done by an agent or servant` OR `the person appears to be employed at the licensed quarry`)
    AND `in the course of the licensee's business`
